From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:31:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: sn201202x: Sleep while idle

An SN201202x stays awake for as long as the system is, even with nothing
attached and nothing to do. On a MacBook Air (13-inch, M4) the SMC reads
about 190 mW on the 3.3 V rail that feeds the two controllers while they
are awake, and about 1 mW once they sleep.

Let an idle controller sleep, with runtime PM: a register access wakes
it, and it sleeps again a second after the last one. Its event interrupt
stays live while it sleeps, so an attach or a power change still reaches
the handler, whose first read wakes it. Nothing else reads the
controller on its own, so it sleeps through charging and with a USB
device attached too. A display, Thunderbolt or USB4 link keeps it awake,
as nothing was tested with one while it sleeps, and so does Apple's DBMa
debug mode. After a few failed tries to sleep, it stays awake until the
next access. System sleep wakes an idle controller before its own SLEEP
handshake, and resume hands it back to runtime PM; one that does not
wake sleeps on through system sleep, without the wakeup watch, and
resume wakes it.

The SPMI bus holds a runtime PM reference while the driver is bound.
Probe gives it to idle sleep only on the T8132 controllers, where the
event interrupt is known to stay live while they sleep, as the system
sleep event filter relies on. Elsewhere it is kept and the controller
stays awake as before. power/autosuspend_delay_ms and power/control
change the delay or turn idle sleep off.

The SN201202x transport test now takes __regmap_sn201202x_read(), the
transfer itself, rather than its new wrapper.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 8e656b0b6979dd4ba074438a6a318dd88d0d3f57)

[j604 backport: probe tail resolved without the latched-event replay (tps->data->irq_handler) of an aurora commit not in omacom 7.2.11; the selftest script is absent here]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
